ncy all for one  should be able to  wake shiguraki up and allow him to break  free  and even if that wasn't the case um if  if shigaraki was brainwashed all for one  could just take over because  you know if you brainwash shigaraki  you're not brainwashing all for one so  he could then come out and take over the  body  so i think whichever way you cut it it's  just not going to work  at this stage against shiguraki to  answer the first part of your question  about shinzo taking a racehead spot  during the battle i know you were just  talking hypothetically but  yeah it wouldn't happen anyway because  shinzo still  is not on the hero course yet the  students are still in their first year  and shinzo isn't joining the hero course  until the second year  so it would be kind of irresponsible to  have a general study student  on the battlefield right now so yeah  he's not going to be involved for the  time being  although you guys know i love shinzo so  i hope he gets a chance to shine  later during this arc the second  question  is most overrated and underrated pro  hero  according to the charts um  okay so most underrated this one's easy  this is obviously izawa  i mean yeah okay so we don't know his  rating but we do know  that he's not in the top ten and he  should be he should be in the top 10.  um so what we know is that izawa is an  underground hero  he doesn't really get much spotlight so  obviously that would affect his ranking  and that's like a personal choice he's  made not to take the spotlight which is  fair enough  but um in my opinion he should be top 10  not just because of  his his insane skill but also his mental  uh his mental fortitude you know because  he he cut his own leg off  without even a second thought and  someone who fearlessly goes into battle  whenever his students are in danger  that's a true hero in my opinion you  know we saw it during the usj attack he  went  head to head with shigaraki and the nomu  during the oval arc he was helping 